  annotation "note_1771582224060_1", anchor: "Warning-marks in Old Pressure-Tongue line the main tunnel. Someone scratched them out.", text: "The Wake-Singers do not read Old Pressure-Tongue. The Collective☽ Of Led∴merch do not read Old Pressure-Tongue. The number of living readers could hold a meeting on my desk without crowding. Whoever defaced these warnings knew what they said — the scratching follows glyph boundaries, not random vandalism. Someone literate enough to parse pre-civilizational script walked into this corridor and decided the warnings were worse than what they warned against. I would very much like to know which word they started with.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582224060_2", anchor: "a child's drawing of something with too many eyes", text: "A child. In deep contested corridors of a corruption-saturated cavern system adjacent to an active breach. Clever Ice Age mining operations brought families into the seams — the labor practices of that era produced more harm than any commemorative plaque will tell you — so it is possible. But I have seen what prolonged corruption exposure does to adult fine motor control, and the result looks very much like a child's hand. The drawing may not indicate the artist's age. Only their duration.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
